WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.290
Okay.

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:07.400
Sometimes it's easy to get a false sense of
security as someone who knows that we are

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.710
in the United States legally with an American
passport.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.860
I was born in Argentina.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.730
I came to the United States, my family had
the a visa lottery.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.260
Uh, and when I was 17 years old, because my
parents were citizens, I was able to go to

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.460
the post office, fill out a passport application
form and that made me an American citizen.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:30.670
So I have a level of comfort, uh, when I'm
talking to police officers or people from

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:36.179
border patrol, if I'm traveling down near
the southern border or whatever, um, that

00:00:36.179 --> 00:00:40.019
is warranted in the sense that I know I'm
here legally, but at the same time it can

00:00:40.019 --> 00:00:42.109
be a false sense of security.

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:47.019
We all the time hear horror stories about
migrants who are detained for days without

00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:48.899
soap, without a toothbrush.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:53.649
But we sometimes think it could never happen
to us because we are here legally.

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:59.359
And then we hear about and nine year old US
citizen with her passport who was detained

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:02.709
by border patrol for 32 hours in March.

00:01:02.709 --> 00:01:08.950
We had one story last week like this, so if
an 18 year old American citizen, a Francisco

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:15.870
Erwin Galicia who was determined the detained
by a border patrol transferred to ice held

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:23.390
for three weeks, even though he had documents
on his person that proved he was born in Texas

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:29.060
within four hours of the Dallas morning news
reporting about it, Galicia was free.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.100
The explanation, it was a so-called bureaucratic
mix-up.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:39.520
Regardless whether detainees do or don't have
American citizenship, they shouldn't be held

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.200
without a shower for 23 days like Galicia
was.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.620
It's UNAMERICAN and it's immoral and it is
the antithesis of what this country is supposed

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.909
to be, but it's even worse.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:55.840
We've now learned of a nine year old girl
who in March was detained by border patrol

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.810
for 32 hours even though she was a US citizen.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.620
I'm talking about Julia Medina.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:03.620
She's American.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.409
Her family lives in Mesut, Mexico.

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:08.459
They cross the border to go to school each
day.

00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:12.499
She and her 14 year old brother were detained
by border patrol.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:18.560
She had her passport on her, but border patrol
said the picture on the passport doesn't really

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:19.580
look like her.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.079
She was questioned at nine years old without
her parents present.

00:02:24.079 --> 00:02:30.260
When border patrol was asked, why did it take
32 hours to confirm her legal status as an

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.010
American citizen?

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:37.029
So far as of an hour ago, border patrol has
not had an explanation.

00:02:37.029 --> 00:02:42.340
Border Patrol tried to have Julia's 14 year
old brother sign a document which said, actually

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:49.790
Juliette is his cousin, not his sister, insinuating
some kind of human trafficking angle to the

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.959
entire fiasco, which of course is untrue.

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:53.870
It was indeed his sister.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:03:00.150
Border Patrol also said Julia provided inconsistent
information during her questioning.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:05.260
She's nine years old, that she first say pizza's
her favorite food and later said that it's

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.260
hot dogs.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:11.829
She's nine years old being questioned by law
enforcement without her parents.

00:03:11.829 --> 00:03:16.840
Eventually Julia's mother was able to get
the help of the Mexican consulate who contacted

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.629
American immigration authorities.

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:24.779
So I'm not telling you this story to suggest
that this would be okay if Julia really wasn't

00:03:24.779 --> 00:03:26.489
a citizen, right?

00:03:26.489 --> 00:03:31.989
This is a moral crisis of the highest level,
no matter what the nationality of the kids

00:03:31.989 --> 00:03:33.470
that are being detained is.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:38.529
What I'm trying to point out to you is that
first of all, of course, this is hugely racially

00:03:38.529 --> 00:03:39.529
tinge.

00:03:39.529 --> 00:03:44.000
She's American with a passport, but she's
non White Hispanic, crossing the border from

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Mexico.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.370
Secondly, if you're angry about how she was
treated, realize that it's just as bad for

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.230
a nine year old without an American passport
to be treated this way.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:58.540
It's really easy for us to sit back and not
react strongly when we're told, listen, a

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.409
lot of these kids in cages and kids being
detained and questioned by law enforcement,

00:04:02.409 --> 00:04:05.360
with no lawyers or parents, a lot of them
are here illegally.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.059
They're not American citizens.

00:04:07.059 --> 00:04:08.799
These are children.

00:04:08.799 --> 00:04:09.799
These are children.

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:11.999
They're not deciding things for themselves.

00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:18.209
If you're horrified by this story of the nine
year old US citizen, Julia Medina, you should

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:23.100
be just as horrified by the stories of non-citizen
kids as well.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.990
Understand the gravity of the direction that
we are going here.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:32.430
This isn't just becoming a papers please society
that we're developing.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:36.020
It's one where even with the papers, it doesn't
help you.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:41.110
Like it didn't help Julia Medina because apparently
as a nine year old, based on the combination

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:47.440
of her quote inconsistent answers and coming
over the border and not looking like the picture

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:54.400
on her passport, even then the papers were
not good enough to prevent a 32 hours attention

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.060
of a nine year old by immigration authorities.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.030
I don't know what the solution is here it
is.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:04.610
I mean, yes, it's obviously getting rid of
Donald Trump and changing the policy around

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:08.160
a lot of what is going on, but that's not
the solution in and of itself.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.400
This is a much bigger problem.

